            <ArticleTitle>[The clinical use of lincomycin in treating anaerobic infection in patients with surgical abdomen].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Experience is recorded with lincomycin treatment of 59 patients with acute surgical abdomen. The primary anaerobic flora was eradicated in 86 per cent of the patients. For the very good therapeutic results essential was the early instituted adequate antibiotic therapy in adequate dose and for adequate length of time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
